dation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R49\",\n    \"edition\": 2013,\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [2]\n  }\n}\n\nWait — the config entries for temperature: axis \"meter_temperature_class\" — but note: all models are available in all four temperature classes? The table lists the classes for each DN table, presumably all variants available in all classes. So config axis is temperature class.\n\nFor the MPE config: axis \"water_temperature\".\n\nRegarding the \"Ø\" characters: \"± 2 (at Ø ≤ 30°C)\". I'll normalize to \"θ ≤ 30 °C\". Fine.\n\nAlso should I include a type_level \"maximum_permitted_error_upper_zone\" with config split? No — config_level only.\n\nOne more: \"Meter temperature class\" row lists T30, T50, T30/70, T70 — also could be captured as type_level list. Skip as reasoned.\n\nAlso \"battery\": the value \"li-battery 3,6 V, life time 16 years\" — I split. Good.\n\nNow the matrix tables details:\n\nTable 1:\n{\n  \"name\": \"Tab. 4 — Model variants for DN 25\",\n  \"columns\": [\"model_id\", \"dn\", \"q3\", \"q1\", \"q2\", \"q4\", \"ratio_q3_q1\", \"ratio_q2_q1\", \"pressure_loss_delta_p\", \"connection_thread\", \"construction_length_l\"],\n  \"column_units\": [null, \"mm\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null, null, \"bar\", null, \"mm\"],\n  \"rows\": [...8 rows...],\n  \"description\": \"Nominal diameter DN 25 (certificate page 7). Four variants at Q3 = 6.3 m³/h and four at Q3 = 10 m³/h, distinguished by ratio Q3/Q1.\",\n  \"footnotes\": []\n}\n\nWait — schema for matrix_tables: name, columns[], rows[] (object per row), description, footnotes[]. column_units shown in the R137 example. I'll include column_units.\n\nRows — should cells be raw numbers or structured? The R137 example uses raw numbers in rows. Good, raw.\n\nTable 2: name \"Tab. 5 — Model variants for DN 32\", 7 rows.\nTable 3: name \"Model variants for DN 40\" (unlabeled Tab. 6 on page 9), 11 rows.\n\nNow the model_level entries. Let me write them fully.\n\n1.\n{\n  \"a